Development-only RAUC signing key and certificate (dev.key.pem / dev.cert.pem),
generated on first use by scripts/gen-dev-keys.sh - `make dev-keys`, which every
build target runs. They are never committed.
The CN says DO NOT USE IN PRODUCTION and it is self-signed; nothing on a device
trusts it once LAAVAT_RAUC_SIGN is on, because the device keyring is the
service's issuing CA (see ../../rauc/).

`rauc bundle` refuses to run without a key, so do_bundle needs one before the
service ever re-signs the result. That is the only reason this exists.

service-ca.pem is shared from here by every tier. system.conf is shared by every
tier whose rauc-conf bbappend prepends ${LAAVAT_DEVKEYS_DIR} first -
sample-qemu-arm64 and sample-variscite-imx8mm keep their own system.conf.

service-ca.pem is a PLACEHOLDER. Its CN says so, and the tiers that share it pin its
digest, so their builds pass with it installed as the device's update root of trust.
That is fine for a build-time demonstration and wrong for anything else: replace the
file and the pin together before a device sees either.
